    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d657">

                <pb facs="0779" n="773" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg773"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/524</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Under Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-08-18">August 18, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Sir Ronald Campbell<anchor n="5" xml:id="d657-f1"/> called to see me this morning
                    at his request.</p>
                <p>The Minister stated that the British Minister at the Vatican had been authorized
                    to make simultaneous approaches to the Cardinal Secretary of State<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d657-f2"/> with other representatives of the United Nations, upon
                    the initiative of the Brazilian Ambassador, to urge that the Vatican do what
                    might be possible publicly to condemn the assassination and abuse by Germany of
                    innocent persons in occupied territories. I told the Minister that the American
                    representative, Mr. Tittmann, had already been authorized to the same
                    effect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >elles</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
